[{:db/id "q-65574/selection/7346ebe1e5d722acf040262ae8e6e53d26ca80a32da08982328df7eef98b7372" :answer/id #uuid "b2a286e4-c84a-58de-b270-c54eddb95ff8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65574/selection/7336f16cf9437bd809ce5e09d7dc666eb175d0cf5c31ff077c77f0542ed57f13" :answer/id #uuid "9969be14-ed57-529f-b3f1-c4d6b54604ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65574/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "8250ef2f-7289-5956-b472-73327e0a40bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65574/selection/219347bb4a6f51134d7f5aff5da33544f44afee934064621ebff9cf9e335ee59" :answer/id #uuid "b70b4a52-6461-5642-a5fe-aee5e2e51693" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65574/selection/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393" :answer/id #uuid "b2726a2e-489b-51dd-990c-aefd7189dd43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65574/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "98df750c-d872-5b24-ad78-2b70b57bf185" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-65574/selection/7336f16cf9437bd809ce5e09d7dc666eb175d0cf5c31ff077c77f0542ed57f13" :answer-field/choices ["q-65574/selection/7346ebe1e5d722acf040262ae8e6e53d26ca80a32da08982328df7eef98b7372" "q-65574/selection/7336f16cf9437bd809ce5e09d7dc666eb175d0cf5c31ff077c77f0542ed57f13" "q-65574/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-65574/selection/219347bb4a6f51134d7f5aff5da33544f44afee934064621ebff9cf9e335ee59" "q-65574/selection/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-65574" :question/id #uuid "1233738d-9980-5519-b543-2a6375658840" :question/math-academy-id "q-65574" :question/problem "Given that the expression $2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x+ϕ)$ with $R>0$, what is the value of $R?$" :question/worked-solution "The sum formula for cosine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x),$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=2 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & ={2}^{2}+{3}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =4+9 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =13 \\\\ R & =\\sqrt{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-65574/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f12d8028-2520-5706-ba49-d67935036af6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-65574"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80135/selection/88bfd75f2d02246855fdaf06f0ab898568bfc6fbb1cead1588be82cad68b1e2c" :answer/id #uuid "82f6df96-b111-5419-bd2a-259f3d9437cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{80}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80135/selection/79646158e731768cad156c41b1acc7e7d3c8f0b1c929111f383ed45a4d9840ee" :answer/id #uuid "c6843a56-169c-5c75-8868-e9c86cab9108" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{20}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80135/selection/cfa59613343dcd1d266f69e78114708e270fc38593403a2183ff722c45bc8c6d" :answer/id #uuid "e9dbb64a-3cac-5b76-afcb-707ed66a1feb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80135/selection/04a957e6e22629a4173a3ba5fec0752e198f21a1bfd1ab3b4e1aaccd930174d3" :answer/id #uuid "df9cb234-eed4-507c-9ec1-9e9aceafae02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{60}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80135/selection/b8903bf0f0c79152fee06a2deb1a952caebfd91f17e1376aeed868afbb728af8" :answer/id #uuid "4cfff3f8-100c-55a5-a281-9de36806e295" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80135/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4ed077ed-e31f-5fb4-aff3-0324418e805a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80135/selection/b8903bf0f0c79152fee06a2deb1a952caebfd91f17e1376aeed868afbb728af8" :answer-field/choices ["q-80135/selection/88bfd75f2d02246855fdaf06f0ab898568bfc6fbb1cead1588be82cad68b1e2c" "q-80135/selection/79646158e731768cad156c41b1acc7e7d3c8f0b1c929111f383ed45a4d9840ee" "q-80135/selection/cfa59613343dcd1d266f69e78114708e270fc38593403a2183ff722c45bc8c6d" "q-80135/selection/04a957e6e22629a4173a3ba5fec0752e198f21a1bfd1ab3b4e1aaccd930174d3" "q-80135/selection/b8903bf0f0c79152fee06a2deb1a952caebfd91f17e1376aeed868afbb728af8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80135" :question/id #uuid "2482eaaf-f514-5577-a783-2f1ca414760f" :question/math-academy-id "q-80135" :question/problem "Given that the expression $5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ)$ with ${0}^{∘}<ϕ<{90}^{∘}$ and $R>0$, what is the value of $ϕ?$" :question/worked-solution "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=5 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{5}{5} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =1 \\\\ ϕ & ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-80135/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c40813-d2aa-5eff-b5dc-69a2f916f865"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80135"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-107562/selection/56b7e6f0ec0c77c6d08087de3f15bc779d6581b3ac0e26484e32ad8dd75ff54c" :answer/id #uuid "90bf3216-1795-5dd4-84c1-b977a28bad0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107562/selection/c36d8e96571cdbf597a19e132beacc2024b3a0b861ce9c1df29a3e6ad67ff94e" :answer/id #uuid "7d2517b1-51f0-58dd-9e23-8c4b5de0d0eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107562/selection/3a39027d6530a1dd904fd0cc078fc05421064e9482bf795d4962fbe927f847f8" :answer/id #uuid "6c05d775-7693-5b44-9b77-3a537e7cc430" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{4})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107562/selection/bdb38cd232d7f06ed3ab9da01b41a14e1c74a7263fce5a00b0fe181b5f92ca6f" :answer/id #uuid "e086b96b-1b4f-5e23-9ec3-d0c9607006f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{2}{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107562/selection/a199ae0eebbba9f253c93c18e8ab98227b67223f111ef9b1d0047ca7c34c8bb6" :answer/id #uuid "5fa2b771-ea79-5f77-8eec-35f63e4bb977" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{3}{4})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107562/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0c9ae66b-6772-58a3-a25b-84917c1a1a1c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-107562/selection/a199ae0eebbba9f253c93c18e8ab98227b67223f111ef9b1d0047ca7c34c8bb6" :answer-field/choices ["q-107562/selection/56b7e6f0ec0c77c6d08087de3f15bc779d6581b3ac0e26484e32ad8dd75ff54c" "q-107562/selection/c36d8e96571cdbf597a19e132beacc2024b3a0b861ce9c1df29a3e6ad67ff94e" "q-107562/selection/3a39027d6530a1dd904fd0cc078fc05421064e9482bf795d4962fbe927f847f8" "q-107562/selection/bdb38cd232d7f06ed3ab9da01b41a14e1c74a7263fce5a00b0fe181b5f92ca6f" "q-107562/selection/a199ae0eebbba9f253c93c18e8ab98227b67223f111ef9b1d0047ca7c34c8bb6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-107562" :question/id #uuid "eb3f02cc-ae8b-5d22-af77-c5a4f4e69173" :question/math-academy-id "q-107562" :question/problem "Given that the expression $4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ)$ with ${0}^{∘}<ϕ<{90}^{∘}$ and $R>0$, what is the value of $ϕ?$" :question/worked-solution "The sum formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=4 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{3}{4}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-107562/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c40813-d2aa-5eff-b5dc-69a2f916f865"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107562"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-107574/selection/b7d0da2dc72437ba82e85d60e4dda61a94beb36a7dbf485503b2eff893f2895e" :answer/id #uuid "91f096e9-4a32-58f2-b77c-743c4f86df53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+0.730)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107574/selection/2cce31497a9d2f5a405f6f7364360df4e682e728a43ef04d3e4797d1d4e86084" :answer/id #uuid "ca64ca4a-1994-599a-86c3-cc5f7134988e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+0.741)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107574/selection/6803ea291adbfb52a56f2354fd87af793b165819e53b57effc39c1b40ab78174" :answer/id #uuid "210f4b85-e971-5daf-af1b-c80a09dfd2b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+0.841)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107574/selection/752588ad22d4f58b4b6e4f32ce34a35641c62735c68775d769df016d69d4c644" :answer/id #uuid "6f8c3630-b06a-5eaf-93e7-3f73d1bf9a03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+0.841)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107574/selection/e3685c9daadb9393c4da88d6d35ce0b0a0a94027c8a25815421a456588a73713" :answer/id #uuid "aaa7b1b1-262f-5f6f-85d7-d9cf27a72f3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+0.730)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107574/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "41b3225e-802b-5dcf-888b-3a423420e7b6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-107574/selection/b7d0da2dc72437ba82e85d60e4dda61a94beb36a7dbf485503b2eff893f2895e" :answer-field/choices ["q-107574/selection/b7d0da2dc72437ba82e85d60e4dda61a94beb36a7dbf485503b2eff893f2895e" "q-107574/selection/2cce31497a9d2f5a405f6f7364360df4e682e728a43ef04d3e4797d1d4e86084" "q-107574/selection/6803ea291adbfb52a56f2354fd87af793b165819e53b57effc39c1b40ab78174" "q-107574/selection/752588ad22d4f58b4b6e4f32ce34a35641c62735c68775d769df016d69d4c644" "q-107574/selection/e3685c9daadb9393c4da88d6d35ce0b0a0a94027c8a25815421a456588a73713"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-107574" :question/id #uuid "016733e0-c899-5c32-9163-e5388a18d61b" :question/math-academy-id "q-107574" :question/problem "$\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x≈$" :question/worked-solution "The sum formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=\\sqrt{5} \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}) \\\\ ϕ & ≈0.730\\,\\text{rad}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.\n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{R}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ & =(\\sqrt{5})^{2}+{2}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =5+4 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =9 \\\\ R & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x≈3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+0.730)\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-107574/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "65b4e8e7-e558-50e7-a1ec-37a6eff77e87"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107574"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-327988/field-1/2d7938b36b9b608f1e882bd61e1f0c4189e0dfa0f27d73e4e30bacb9a2a85078" :answer/id #uuid "95528d27-c43e-59c3-bbfd-8fd5e06bfc7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{21}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327988/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b380ce15-728c-52bd-882e-468ca1776de4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-327988/field-1/2d7938b36b9b608f1e882bd61e1f0c4189e0dfa0f27d73e4e30bacb9a2a85078" :answer-field/choices ["q-327988/field-1/2d7938b36b9b608f1e882bd61e1f0c4189e0dfa0f27d73e4e30bacb9a2a85078"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-327988/field-2/a8518d54bd12d6a2cd9ba0ff2272e466e986759756afb13c5e03582783bb3ffd" :answer/id #uuid "9d51e50a-143e-5477-be9d-b3394c15a0a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.061" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327988/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "81b2e1eb-9698-563f-8755-97414cd6b848" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-327988/field-2/a8518d54bd12d6a2cd9ba0ff2272e466e986759756afb13c5e03582783bb3ffd" :answer-field/choices ["q-327988/field-2/a8518d54bd12d6a2cd9ba0ff2272e466e986759756afb13c5e03582783bb3ffd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-327988" :question/id #uuid "383887c5-bb2b-5b2e-b8c0-e85d6d548c3c" :question/math-academy-id "q-327988" :question/problem "Express $\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)$ in the form $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x-ϕ)$ with $ϕ\\in (0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ Use the **exact value** for $R,$ and round $ϕ$ to **three decimal places**.\n\n$\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)\\,≈\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x\\,-$\n{{field-2}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x).\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x),$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=\\sqrt{5} \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ ϕ & =arctan\\,(\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}})≈1.061\\text{ }\\text{rad},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.\n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)^{2}+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)^{2} & =(\\sqrt{5})^{2}+{4}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =5+16 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =21 \\\\ R & =\\sqrt{21}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)≈\\sqrt{21}\\,sin\\,(6x-1.061).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-327988/field-1" "q-327988/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "65b4e8e7-e558-50e7-a1ec-37a6eff77e87"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-327988"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
